          ],
          "bullets": [
            "OpenAI rolled out two products in its Daybreak security platform on 12 November, The Register reports: Daybreak Red Team, available in early access, which uses OpenAI models to test companies' web applications for vulnerabilities, and Daybreak Defense Factory, which automates finding, validating and fixing vulnerabilities at scale.",
            "Nancy Wang, who leads cyber-applied AI at OpenAI, described Red Team as \"superhuman pen-test at the scale of automated continuous scanning,\" with a fleet of agents using source code and app context to investigate and test attack paths. Defense Factory agents are built on GPT-6 Cyber and produce what Wang called a merge-ready pull request with the patch and a test that shows that it works.",
            "OpenAI President Greg Brockman said in a Thursday keynote: \"We're now at a point where companies will be secure only to the extent of the frontier model that they use to defend themselves and how well they utilize that.\"",
            "No detection, patch-quality or false-positive figures were published with the launch, and OpenAI's own article page for the announcement could not be opened for this edition. The claims are the company's and are not independently verified."
