          ],
          "bullets": [
            "The Justice Department said on 12 November that FaceStealer, a North Korean social-engineering scheme relying on surreptitiously recorded videos and deepfakes, has resulted in the theft of more than $400 million in the last 18 months. Hackers invite targets to video meetings from previously stolen accounts, record the target's webcam, play prerecorded videos of people the target knows, then claim a technical error and prompt the target to install malware.",
            "Under a federal warrant the FBI seized over 900 webcam videos of FaceStealer victims. The Department names the actors publicly as Sapphire Sleet, UNC1069, Dangerous Password, CryptoCore, APT38, BlueNoroff and Stardust Chollima, and says the scheme has also targeted open-source software developers in a way that appears calculated to enable software supply-chain attacks.",
            "Separately, the Department said members of the North Korean military, which the FBI calls TraderTraitor, stole more than $6 billion worth of virtual assets from Binance on or about 29 October. Collective government and private-sector efforts have frozen more than $2.7 billion, and the Department has obtained court authorization to seize or restrain in excess of $1.2 billion of that amount.",
            "The press release describes the deepfake tooling in unusual terms, saying the hackers use \"super intelligence (SI)\" to create deepfake videos of well-known, influential people. It does not name the models or services used, and The Record reports that efforts to trace and forfeit the remaining assets are ongoing."
